{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumDyPpXPsPHmd784V5y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, but only through gradual deployments, and with caveats. Cloudflare supports gradual rollouts (`wrangler versions upload`, then `wrangler versions deploy` with a percentage split, e.g. 90% old / 10% new). That keeps the old version serving part of your traffic for as long as you choose. However, Durable Objects have a limitation: a given DO instance runs one version at a time, and gradual deployments don't let you split a DO's code across versions in the same way as stateless Workers. Also, a plain `wrangler deploy` goes to 100% immediately, and DOs get restarted onto the new code.\n\nGradual deployments also can't be used when the release includes a DO migration (such as new classes, renames, or deletes). Those need a full deploy. I'm going from memory here, so please check the current Cloudflare docs on \"Gradual deployments\" and Durable Objects, since the details have changed over time."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2262,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2262},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b6979ef-9499-419d-8379-ebe5e3feea45","uuid":"915a7a30-39a3-4a92-9e33-401a1e96c069","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:46:19.173Z","request_id":"req_011CfumDy9wABnAv5xngudpZ"}
